                <p rendition="#center">*CHARTS AND MAPS TO MEMORIAL AND REPLY.<seg type="margin"
                        >[120]</seg></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">A.</hi> Photograph of Map of de Haro. 1790. (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">See page</hi> 17.)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">B.</hi> Photograph of Map of Eliza. 1791. (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">See page</hi> 17.)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">C.</hi> Photograph of Map of Vancouver. 1798. (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">See page</hi> 15.)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">D.</hi> Photograph of Map of Galiano and Valdes. 1802.
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">See page</hi> 17.)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">E.</hi> Photograph of Map of Duflot de Mofras. 1844 (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">See page</hi> 15.)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">F.</hi> Photograph of Map of Wilkes. 1845. (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">See page</hi> 11.)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">G.</hi> Photograph of Map of W. Sturgis. 1845. (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">See page</hi> 9.)</p>
                <pb facs="0220" n="190" xml:id="pg190"/>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">H.</hi> Lithograph of U. S. Coast Survey Map of
                    Washington Sound and Approaches. (<hi rendition="#italic">See end of the
                        volume.</hi>)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">J.</hi> Lithograph of Map of de Haro. 1790. (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">See end of the volume.</hi>)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">K.</hi> Lithograph of Map of Eliza. 1791. (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">See end of the volume.</hi>)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">L.</hi> Lithograph of Spanish Chart published in 1795.
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">See end of the volume.</hi>)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">M.</hi> Cross Sections of Haro and Rosario Channels. (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">See page</hi> 130.)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">N.</hi> Sketch to illustrate the route of the vessels of
                    the Hudson’s Bay Company. (<hi rendition="#italic">See page</hi> 126.)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">O.</hi> Copy of Map <hi rendition="#italic">H</hi>, with
                    a blue line drawn southerly from the center of the Gulf of Georgia in latitude
                    49°; with red lines to show the channels through Haro northward; and a yellow
                    line to show the so-called Rosario Channel. (<hi rendition="#italic">See end of
                        the volume.</hi>)</p>
